+/// The frame an IPC request comes from.
+///
+/// A runtime that knows it puts it into the extensions of the `http::Request` handed to the
+/// `ipc` custom protocol or to the [`WebviewIpcHandler`]. Extensions do not travel with the
+/// request bytes, so a page cannot forge them, unlike the request headers. A request without
+/// it counts as [`Self::Main`]: only runtimes that never accept IPC from subframes may leave it out.
